<section class="sub-hero"><div class="sub-hero-ph" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consultation-laptop.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-laptop-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation-laptop.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap sub-hero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/free-tools/">Free tools</a></li><li aria-current="page">Appraisal Readiness Checkup</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Free checklist</p><h1>Appraisal Readiness Checkup: An Insurance Appraisal Checklist</h1><p class="lede">A strong appraisal starts with a complete file. Work through this insurance appraisal checklist to see what you already have and what to gather first.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Appraisal readiness checkup</span><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation that coverage is accepted. If the claim was denied outright, talk with a Minnesota attorney before thinking about appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask the adjuster in writing for the full itemized estimate, not just the payment summary."><span>Do you have the insurer’s complete, line-item estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get a line-item estimate from a contractor or estimator. A one-line bid is hard to defend before a panel."><span>Do you have your own itemized estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Collect every photo and note when each was taken. Photograph current conditions too, including attic and interior stains."><span>Do you have dated photos from soon after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find ‘Appraisal’ in the policy conditions and note any notice, timing or selection requirements."><span>Have you read the appraisal paragraph in your policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Suit Against Us’ condition and put the date on your calendar. The timeline planner can export it."><span>Do you know your suit-limitation date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Tarp, dry out and protect the property, and keep every invoice and receipt."><span>Were temporary repairs made, with receipts kept?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure wet insulation, ceilings, decking and wall cavities were inspected so the scope is complete."><span>Has hidden damage been opened up and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request the declarations page showing limits and deductibles."><span>Do you have your current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Put emails, letters and claim notes in date order in one folder."><span>Is your correspondence organized by date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the claim gap & fee estimator. A small gap may not justify appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap more than roughly 10% or several thousand dollars?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="If a proof of loss was requested, complete and return it within the stated time."><span>If the insurer asked for a sworn proof of loss, was it sent on time?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out ready-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#e3eef6" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#52c9e8" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3" style="transition:stroke-dashoffset .5s,stroke .3s"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul data-o="todo" class="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="tool-note">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>Why readiness matters</h2>
<p>An appraisal award signed by two of the three panel members is binding on the amount of loss. If photos, hidden damage or an itemized estimate are missing when the panel decides, there may be no second chance to add them. This insurance appraisal checklist helps you catch gaps early.</p>
<h2>How the score is weighted</h2>
<p>Questions that decide whether appraisal is even the right path — accepted coverage, two itemized estimates — count three points. Documentation counts two. Housekeeping items count one. A high score doesn’t mean you’ll win; it means the file is complete enough to argue the number.</p>
<h2>What to do with your to-do list</h2>
<ul>
<li>Work from the top: the heavier items unlock the rest.</li>
<li>Send written requests to the insurer, and keep copies.</li>
<li>Use the timeline planner so deadlines don’t slip while you gather records.</li>
</ul>
<p>Your answers are not stored or sent anywhere.</p>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What score do I need before invoking appraisal?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>There’s no official threshold. A low score means important evidence may be missing; fix those items first or ask a professional to review the file.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I invoke appraisal if coverage is disputed?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Appraisal decides the amount of loss, not coverage. If the insurer has denied coverage, speak with a Minnesota attorney first.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does a high score guarantee a better award?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. It only means the file is well documented. Awards depend on the facts, the estimates and the panel.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free tools</h2><div class="related"><a href="/free-tools/roof-snow-load-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Roof Snow Load Calculator</span><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/free-tools/claim-gap-fee-estimator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Claim Gap &amp; Fee Estimator</span><svg class="i" width="20" height="2